WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.247 --> 00:00:01.500
(pensive music)

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.120
- Everyone thinks of Wyoming,
it's the cowboy state,

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.090
so you think of open
land, cattle and cowboys.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.980
They want it to be open land, cattle,

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.600
cowboys and crypto.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.340
- [Narrator] This 40-acre plot of land

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.900
in northwestern Wyoming has a new owner,

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.650
a group of around 6,000 crypto investors

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.370
whose goal is to build a city
using the Ethereum blockchain.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.710
- We're imagining this kind of future

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.200
where you see this beautiful parcel map

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.020
of all the different pieces of land.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.357
In one click, basically
you just buy this NFT

00:00:30.357 --> 00:00:33.140
and you now have the
right to use that land.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.680
- [Narrator] This group of
investors is called CityDAO

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.470
and it has no official leader.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.170
Rather, it's owned and
governed by its members.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.260
- We are collectively governing this land,

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.590
so we're deciding what
happens to the land.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.660
If we're going to build things,

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.440
if we're gonna allow
people to camp on the land.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.750
- [Narrator] This type of organization

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.970
is known as a DAO.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:55.690
There are about 200 tracked by
the data service DeepDAO

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.320
and they all have different goals.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.650
Like collectively owning an NBA team,

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.150
a rare copy of the US Constitution,

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.630
or a future blockchain-based city.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.580
So how exactly do DAOs work?

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:09.050
Why have they become a part
of Wyoming real estate?

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.273
And what risks come
with investing in them?

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.920
- DAO stands for decentralized
autonomous organization.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.640
Think about a mutual fund,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.880
which is an investment
product created by a company,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.390
the company maintains it,

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:25.300
the company is responsible
for managing all the money,

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.150
for deciding what the
mutual fund's purpose is,

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.110
what its goal is.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.720
- [Narrator] But unlike a mutual fund,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.340
DAOs don't have a company

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.510
or any leader to make these decisions.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.820
Instead, members pool money together

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:37.940
and decide as a group

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.460
how they want to spend it.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.140
Usually once members buy in,

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.080
they receive a token, which
grants them voting rights.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.100
All of the DAO's
functions are also written

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.760
into code on the blockchain.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.403
- Think about an investment vehicle

00:01:49.403 --> 00:01:53.530
where all the components
of the investment vehicle

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.080
are written into a piece
of software and launched,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.250
and nobody actually owns it

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.120
and it runs out on its own.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.930
- [Narrator] Unlike a
traditional corporate structure

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.550
where the company looks for
investors to raise money,

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.420
DAOs let people find them
through the internet.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.330
- The real sort of
ingenious idea behind this

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.410
isn't necessarily that you come up

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:16.660
with some new way to make money.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.030
It's that you've come up with a new way

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.974
to find investors.

00:02:19.974 --> 00:02:22.190
- [Narrator] CityDAO became
the first DAO to own land

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.910
thanks to a new law in Wyoming

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.950
that went into effect last July.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.497
The law recognizes DAOs as LLCs

00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:30.820
and LLCs can own real estate.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.220
- Wyoming passed this law

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:35.610
because Wyoming legislators
a couple of years ago decided

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.960
that blockchain could give the
state a competitive advantage

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.030
and they wanted to try

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:42.830
to attract blockchain-based businesses.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.840
- [Narrator] Wyoming has
passed a number of laws

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.990
to make it easier for
blockchain-based companies

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.270
to operate out of the state,

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.170
one of which exempts
cryptocurrency from state tax.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:54.210
Inspired by the Wyoming DAO law,

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.200
Scott Fitsimones started CityDAO

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.900
in the hopes that eventually people

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.690
could buy land instantaneously

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.480
and those transactions
would be transparent

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.430
for all to see on the blockchain.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.660
- If you were to go want to buy

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.170
or build something on a piece
of land in Wyoming right now,

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.320
you would have to go to LoopNet,

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.611
you'd have to go explore
different pieces of land,

00:03:12.611 --> 00:03:14.150
you'd have to go on Craigslist

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.840
and try to call people,

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.860
and work out a deal, sign some papers,

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:18.910
maybe mail something.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.680
It would just be a very
cumbersome, tiresome process.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.050
- [Narrator] Fitsimones says CityDAO

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.180
has raised around $7 million

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.850
from its membership since
it was founded last July.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.780
Members include Brian Armstrong,

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.030
the co-founder of Coinbase,

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:35.230
and Vitalik Buterin, co-creator
of the Ethereum network.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.350
To join CityDAO,

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.340
you have to buy a citizen NFT,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.370
which currently sells
for about 0.4 Ethereum,

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.400
which is around $1,000.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.530
Once you're a citizen,

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.330
you have the right to vote on proposals

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.020
and propose your own ideas.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.620
- For example, we had citizens
already pass a proposal

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.520
to get drone footage of the land.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.820
- [Narrator] In January,
CityDAO released a new batch

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.850
of NFTs for citizens to purchase.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.390
Each one represents a lease

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:00.870
to a specific plot of land in Wyoming.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.670
- So imagine CityDAO
LLC owns this property

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:08.120
but we basically encode a lease as an NFT

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.530
and say you have the
right to use this parcel,

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:12.950
build on this parcel.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.460
- [Narrator] Fitsimones says they intend

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.670
to treat this parcel as a test run

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:17.710
and that they're already looking

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:19.680
at locations for their next purchase.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:22.260
He says the next one will
be in a less remote area,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.750
so citizens can have the option

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.060
to build on the land.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.030
- Perhaps there's some future

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.320
where we start living there,
living close to each other,

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.830
building things on the land.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.280
- [Narrator] He also says CityDAO

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.960
is looking into buying
land outside Wyoming.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.980
- We would still use the Wyoming LLC

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.890
and technically, Wyoming
LLCs can own land anywhere

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.419
but there are certainly some nuances

00:04:40.419 --> 00:04:43.720
to how that works.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.930
- [Narrator] DAOs are still considered

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.430
an experimental business model,

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.010
even as awareness grows.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.440
- I think DAOs are
going to remain limited.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.220
I think the idea is very intriguing.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.480
I think you will see a lot of
attempts at experimentation.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.510
People are gonna try it
out, see where it fits

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:02.280
but I think for the time being,

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.140
it's gonna be really hard to do one

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:07.090
of these on a very, very large scale.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.370
- [Narrator] One DAO that made headlines

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.680
in November was ConstitutionDAO.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.150
It tried to buy a rare first edition copy

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:14.620
of the US Constitution,

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.080
raising over $40 million
in less than a week.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.930
That's just one example of how DAOs

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:22.430
can raise a lot of capital very quickly.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:25.410
But this also makes them
a big target for hacking.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.378
- When you're doing this,

00:05:26.378 --> 00:05:29.240
ultimately, everything
now becomes dependent

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.520
upon the software.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.080
If it was not written well

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.780
and it collects a lot of money,

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.840
somebody's gonna figure
out a way to hack it,

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.800
and get into it.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:40.230
I mean, even well-written
software programs

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.140
can be hacked.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.000
- [Narrator] And because
most DAOs communicate

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.040
through the messaging platform Discord,

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.360
security there is a growing
area of concern as well.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.300
On January 10th, someone hacked

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.990
into a CityDAO administrator's
account on Discord

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:55.330
and scammed some members
into sending them tens

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.810
of thousands of dollars.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:58.760
Fitsimones said that after the incident,

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.770
CityDAO did a full review
and increased security

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:02.603
on its server.

00:06:02.603 --> 00:06:04.540
He added that this type of attack

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.900
has been happening to several DAO servers.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.650
A spokeswoman from Discord
says the company is working

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:12.730
to prevent scams by investing
significant resources

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:15.890
in education and tools
that protect its users.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.950
The lack of a traditional
corporate structure

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.300
could also make it harder

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.940
for individual investors
to hold DAOs accountable

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.920
when it comes to fraud, scams and abuse.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:29.920
- This is a very risky, very nascent space

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.250
and most of the people who are in it sort

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:36.380
of understand those risks
and are willing to take them.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.020
- [Narrator] The SEC says it wants

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.840
to bring the digital currency market

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.230
under its investor protection framework.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.720
Meanwhile, DAO enthusiasts like Fitsimones

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:47.900
are hopeful that DAOs will
improve and grow over time.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.710
- Eventually, people will kind

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.520
of realize the existing system

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:55.050
of it takes a month to buy
a piece of land or property,

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.310
that will seem really crazy.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.930
And I definitely imagine
more and more land

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.220
and assets coming onto the blockchain

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.740
and CityDAO being there when that happens

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.934
and helping make it all possible.

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:08.601
(pensive music)

